First, let's find an expression for $G'(x)$ in terms of $f'$ and $h'$:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}G'(x)
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}G(x)&&\gray{\text{Equivalent notation}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}[3f(x)-2h(x)+6]&&\gray{\text{Substitute the expression for }G(x)}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}[3f(x)]-\dfrac{d}{dx}[2h(x)]+\dfrac{d}{dx}(6)&&\gray{\text{Sum and difference rules}}
\\\\
&=3f'(x)-2h'(x)+0&&\gray{\text{Constant and constant multiple rules}}
\end{align}$

So we found that $G'(x)=3f'(x)-2h'(x)$.
